;; The REPL (PY5e; survey §6.1): python3's basic REPL on the process's standard input, prompts (sys.ps1,
;; sys.ps2) on stderr. Each interactive statement is compiled by the host in mode "single": its
;; expression statements display their value through sys.displayhook (repr, bound to builtins._); a
;; statement that needs more lines ("incomplete", codeop's rule: an open bracket or block, a compound
;; statement until a blank line) reads them. An exception is printed and the session goes on; SystemExit
;; ends it with its status; end of input ends it with status 0.

